Intelligent Loan Advisor & Policy Assistant:
This project is called Intelligent Loan Advisor & Policy Assistant, a Generative AI-powered banking assistant designed to help users obtain loan-related information through natural language conversations.

The primary objective of this solution is to simplify access to banking information such as loan eligibility criteria, interest rate policies, KYC requirements, required documents, and loan guidelines. Instead of manually searching through lengthy policy documents, users can simply ask questions in natural language and receive accurate answers.

The architecture follows a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) approach.

The process begins when a user submits a query through the user interface developed using Streamlit. The request is then sent to a FastAPI backend, which manages the application logic.

On the knowledge side, banking policy documents are collected and processed. These documents are divided into smaller chunks, converted into vector embeddings, and stored in a vector database such as FAISS or ChromaDB.

When a user asks a question, the query is also converted into an embedding. The system performs a similarity search in the vector database to identify the most relevant document sections related to the user's query.

The retrieved information is then combined with the user's question and passed to the Large Language Model through the RAG pipeline. Using both the retrieved context and its language understanding capabilities, the model generates an accurate and context-aware response.

Finally, the generated answer, along with the reference source information, is displayed to the user.

The key technologies used in this project include Python, FastAPI, Streamlit, LangChain, Vector Databases, Embeddings, Retrieval-Augmented Generation, and Large Language Models.

One of the major advantages of this approach is that it significantly reduces hallucination by grounding responses in actual banking documents. It also improves answer accuracy, transparency, and user trust by providing source-based responses.



Banking Customer Chat Assistant:
This project is called Banking Customer Chat Assistant, an AI-powered customer support solution developed using Python, Streamlit, FastAPI, and LangGraph.

The main objective of this project is to automate customer support operations in the banking domain by providing quick, accurate, and secure responses to customer queries.

The system follows a multi-agent architecture, where different AI agents are responsible for handling specific banking services.

The user interacts with the system through a Streamlit-based chat interface. When a query is submitted, it is sent to the FastAPI backend, which manages the request processing and agent orchestration.

The first step is Intent Classification. The customer's message is analyzed to identify the user's requirement, such as account information, card services, loan inquiries, dispute status, complaints, or policy-related questions.

Based on the identified intent, the request is routed by LangGraph to the appropriate specialized agent.

For example:

The Account Agent handles balance and account-related inquiries.
The Card Agent manages card-related services such as blocking or reporting lost cards.
The Loan Agent provides loan details and status information.
The Dispute Agent handles transaction disputes and dispute tracking.
The Complaint Agent assists in complaint registration.
The RAG Agent retrieves information from banking documents and knowledge bases to answer policy-related questions.

A key feature of the solution is the implementation of risk-based routing and guardrails.

Before executing any action, the system evaluates the risk level of the request. Sensitive operations such as money transfers, PIN changes, or card blocking are classified as high-risk activities and are restricted or redirected according to banking policies.

Guardrails are used to validate user inputs, prevent unauthorized actions, enforce security policies, and ensure that responses remain safe, compliant, and reliable.

For knowledge-related queries, the system uses a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline. Relevant information is retrieved from the knowledge base and provided to the language model, enabling accurate and context-aware responses while reducing hallucinations.

The major technologies used in this project include:

Python
Streamlit
FastAPI
LangGraph
Large Language Models (LLMs)
Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
Vector Databases
Prompt Engineering
REST APIs
Git and Docker

The key benefits of this solution are:

Automated customer support
Faster response times
Multi-agent task specialization
Secure request handling
Risk-aware decision making
Reduced hallucinations through RAG
Improved customer experience and operational efficiency




