AI-Enhanced Data Structure Visualization with Real-Time Execution.:
This project is called AI-Enhanced Data Structure Visualization with Real-Time Execution. It is a full-stack web application developed to help users understand how sorting algorithms work through interactive visualizations and real-time execution.

The main objective of this project was to make learning data structures and algorithms more engaging and easier to understand by visually demonstrating each step of algorithm execution.

The application consists of a frontend built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript and a backend developed using Python with FastAPI and Flask. The communication between the frontend and backend is handled through REST APIs using JSON-based data exchange.

When a user provides input data and selects a sorting algorithm, the request is sent to the backend through an API call. The backend executes the selected algorithm and returns step-by-step execution data to the frontend.

The frontend visualizes the sorting process in real time, allowing users to see how elements are compared, swapped, and arranged until the final sorted output is achieved.

The platform supports performance analysis by tracking important metrics such as:

Execution time
Number of comparisons
Number of swaps
Algorithm efficiency

One of the key features of this project is the AI-based algorithm recommendation system.

Based on factors such as input size and data characteristics, the system intelligently recommends the most suitable sorting algorithm for better performance and learning purposes.

