AI Citizen Assist: Smart Scheme Recommender with Analytics.
This project is called AI Citizen Assist: Smart Scheme Recommender with Analytics. It is an end-to-end AI-powered platform developed to help citizens discover government schemes that match their eligibility and needs.

The main objective of this project is to simplify access to government welfare schemes and ensure that citizens can easily identify benefits they are entitled to without manually searching through multiple websites and documents.

The solution is developed using Python and integrates multiple technologies, including live API data retrieval, intelligent recommendation engines, analytics, and multi-agent orchestration.

The process begins when a user provides personal information such as age, gender, occupation, income level, education, location, and other eligibility details.

The system fetches the latest scheme information from available data sources and APIs. It then performs eligibility matching, where citizen details are compared against the criteria of various government schemes.

To improve recommendation accuracy, the platform uses an intelligent scoring mechanism. Each scheme is assigned a score based on how well it matches the user's profile and requirements.

The system not only recommends individual schemes but also suggests personalized combinations of schemes, helping users maximize the benefits available to them.

A key feature of this project is the use of multi-agent orchestration.

Different agents work together to perform specific tasks:

Data Retrieval Agent retrieves scheme information.
Eligibility Agent validates user eligibility.
Ranking Agent prioritizes the most relevant schemes.
Analytics Agent generates insights and visual reports.
Document Generation Agent prepares user-friendly reports and summaries.

The platform also generates visual analytics dashboards that help users understand recommendations through charts, graphs, and summarized insights.

